      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step says, “The norm is continuous and r↦r^{-p} is continuous on r>0 by [F2].” F2’s cited real-power result establishes continuity of positive-base real powers, while the Euclidean supplier defines ‖x‖₂ = √⟨x,x⟩ without stating its continuity. Thus [F2] does not license the norm-continuity clause used for Borel measurability. The gap is readily filled from the coordinate formula, so it is nonfatal.",
